# port-patches.sh: keep-p0 @ 820d104ac9ac over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits 6cc5c62a69ae..3c8b05d8bbb7); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: the race's margin is relative past 1, and TF_GLM_NUCLEUS_RACE_CHECK=1 draws every raced row again from whole shards

Review: an absolute 1e-9 rounds back to the bound once |score| passes 2^24 (temperature near its 1e-6 clamp), so the
margin is 1e-9 * max(1, |bound|). The check mode compares the race's tokens with the whole-shard draw's bit for bit on
the device (error.RaceMismatch), for GPU receipts; the u range comment now says u can be 1 (+inf scores, as the host).

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0037-zig-glm-nucleus-race-check.patch

